0.9193342924118042,"text_excerpt":"This place is a gem! Located in not the best area some would say but it's full of charm. They have a bar and games as well to keep you occupied during your stay. Between the 3 of us we had the Perogis, strogonoff, veggie bilini, and chicken noodle soup, stuffed cabbage, burger and beer cheese fries. Everything was delicious and priced amazing! 10/10 would go back!!"},{"business_id":"MziuWnUVrnx8R4J4e_QOrQ","review_id":"CU9URWjbvzwHaB_fqJmLfQ","date":"2019-12-25T21:43:30","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9180054664611816,"text_excerpt":"I love this place for the variety and quality of the food. The prices are good and the beer selection is great. Staff is super, esp Jill. It's a great spot to drop into for comfort food."},{"business_id":"MziuWnUVrnx8R4J4e_QOrQ","review_id":"GJFp4VyCkC-lCsABKvna4g","date":"2019-12-17T01:20:05","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9120354652404785,"text_excerpt":"Tasty, quality food, & great deals! I tried their borscht the other night and was pleased with it. The spices were interesting... different than my own recipe in that I tasted more cinnamon or nutmeg than the usual dill. Still very good though, and it comes with a nice little garlic roll. Only $6 a bowl! Also tried the fries and there were so many, I shared with the rest of the table. Good crisp \"real\" fries, as my friend put it. Again, only $2.50! My friends got sandwiches and pierogis, and I was heavily envying the latter. Please, Green Room... if you read this... add a vegan pierogi to the menu. Cheese messes me up, but damn, I love them."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
